## Bug

In `reserve()` (doc: *"Takes qty units if that many are left; returns whether it did."*), the availability check used `<=` instead of `<`:

```4:8:/tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/inventory.ts
export function reserve(sku: string, qty: number): boolean {
	const have = stock.get(sku) ?? 0;
	if (have <= qty) { return false; }
	stock.set(sku, have - qty);
	return true;
}
```

This incorrectly rejected the valid case where `have == qty` (exactly enough stock to fully reserve), even though the doc says it should succeed whenever "that many are left."

## Fix

```diff
- if (have <= qty) { return false; }
+ if (have < qty) { return false; }
```

(line 6 of `/tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/inventory.ts`)

Now `reserve` only fails when there's strictly less stock than requested, matching the doc comment.

Confirmed: `reserve` returns `false` on insufficient stock, but `checkout` just `continue`s instead of throwing the documented error.## Bug

In `/tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/checkout.ts`, the doc comment states `checkout` should throw `'out of stock <sku>'` when a sku can't be reserved:

```3:3:/tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/checkout.ts
/** Reserves every sku (throws 'out of stock <sku>' when one can't be), then returns the cart total. */
```

But the implementation silently `continue`d instead of throwing when `reserve(sku, qty)` returned `false` (out of stock), so unavailable items were just skipped rather than causing an error.

## Fix

```diff
--- a/src/checkout.ts
+++ b/src/checkout.ts
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ export function checkout(cart: Cart, skus: Array<[string, number]>, discountPc
 	for (const [sku, qty] of skus) {
-		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }
+		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { throw new Error(`out of stock ${sku}`); }
 	}
 	return cart.total(discountPct);
 }
```

Line 6 now throws an `Error` with message `` out of stock ${sku} `` instead of swallowing the failed reservation, matching the doc comment. Only `src/checkout.ts` was modified.
